    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Pilgrimage is the third studio album by American drone metal band Om and their first release for Southern Lord, arriving at a pivotal moment in the group’s evolution. Recorded at Electrical Audio with Steve Albini, the album captures the stripped-down power that would define Om’s early work: massive bass lines, disciplined drumming, and a hypnotic, mantra-like focus that turns repetition into momentum. It is also the final Om studio album to feature drummer Chris Hakius, giving the record added significance within the band’s catalog.\n\nAcross its four extended tracks — including the title piece, “Unitive Knowledge of the Godhead,” and “Bhima’s Theme” — Pilgrimage balances heaviness with a meditative, כמעט ritualistic atmosphere. The result is one of Om’s most celebrated releases, often regarded as a key statement of their sound: austere, immersive, and spiritually charged, yet anchored by a tight, physical groove. Its reception has remained strong enough to keep it in demand, underscoring its status as a defining album in modern heavy music.",
